{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1354762-playing-2e-without-touchstones","id":1354762,"title":"Playing 2e Without Touchstones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-13T07:09:38-08:00","id":1354762,"title":"Playing 2e Without Touchstones","content":"I'm getting ready to run my first 2e game, and I keep going over the section of the rulebook concerning Touchstones and wondering why I should bother with them. To my eyes, they don't add much in terms of needed flavor, and it seems like a person could just lift that whole set of rules (including both the benefits of having Touchstones and the penalties for not having any) out without affecting the gameplay in any significant way. Am I missing something crucial here? Has anyone tried playing without these rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T07:28:57-08:00","id":1354767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gscrap</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1354762-playing-2e-without-touchstones#post1354762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting ready to run my first 2e game, and I keep going over the section of the rulebook concerning Touchstones and wondering why I should bother with them. To my eyes, they don't add much in terms of needed flavor, and it seems like a person could just lift that whole set of rules (including both the benefits of having Touchstones and the penalties for not having any) out without affecting the gameplay in any significant way. Am I missing something crucial here? Has anyone tried playing without these rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from bonuses/penalties for Clarity damage rolls changing the rate at which you gain Clarity damage, and the consequences of losing Touchstones, you lose <i>one of two ways to heal Clarity damage</i>, which could be pretty significant. How significant, I couldn't tell you because I haven't experienced the difference in play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T09:32:15-08:00","id":1354782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1354762-playing-2e-without-touchstones?p=1354767#post1354767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aside from bonuses/penalties for Clarity damage rolls changing the rate at which you gain Clarity damage, and the consequences of losing Touchstones, you lose <i>one of two ways to heal Clarity damage</i>, which could be pretty significant. How significant, I couldn't tell you because I haven't experienced the difference in play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Building on this, losing Touchstones deprives you specifically of the means of healing Clarity damage that doesn't require you to have dropped to the level where <i>every time you take more Clarity damage, you take a Condition and possibly risk becoming Comatose</i>.<br /> <br /> The only way to get back above Clarity 3 without spending time with Touchstones, acquiring new Icons, or getting the help of someone with a specific Royal Contract is to resolve <i>Persistent</i> Clarity Conditions. This is a substantially dangerous game to be playing, since the odds of still having attached Touchstones to mitigate the damage are quite low and Persistent Clarity Conditions are roughly equal in weight to the Conditions you get from dramatically failing an Integrity breaking point. Even then, your Clarity is still effectively capped at the level where penalties are happening.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T09:43:37-08:00","id":1354783,"title":"","content":"Touchstones are absolutely key to the 2e Clarity system. If you remove them, you need to replace them with some other easily accessible means of healing Clarity damage.<br /> <br /> Other games have Touchstones which aren't so central to their systems. You can lift Touchstones out of Requiem or Forsaken pretty easily. Changeling and Deviant lean on them heavily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 12-13-2019, 12:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T09:57:19-08:00","id":1354785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1354762-playing-2e-without-touchstones?p=1354783#post1354783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other games have Touchstones which aren't so central to their systems. You can lift Touchstones out of Requiem or Forsaken pretty easily. Changeling and Deviant lean on them heavily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Removing Touchstones from Requiem dramatically increases the rate of frenzy and/or killing, because they're the only other way of resolving the Tempted and Jaded Conditions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-13T12:29:02-08:00","id":1354805,"title":"","content":"Forsaken is the only 2e that uses Touchstones where I'd even consider removing them, and that's mostly because unlike the rest you can adjust your Harmony rating by purposefully performing breaking points in the direction you want it to move.<br /> <br /> When your Integrity equivalent is &quot;high good, low bad&quot; Touchstones are inherently useful, and good story hooks. Even if they might not feel as essential in some games than others, they're worth having (and you get at least one for free anyway).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T07:11:44-08:00","id":1355176,"title":"","content":"Thanks all for the feedback. I guess I'll have to give some more thought to how I can fill the gap in Clarity restoration before I take the step of writing out Touchstones. I think I'd prefer if that could be accomplished by multiple different kinds of interactions with the mortal world rather than just one (without spending merit dots) but I haven't really considered what that would look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12108-gscrap","name":"gscrap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12108_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:47:09-08:00","id":1355237,"title":"","content":"Aside from just the mechanical argument, I find Touchstones a great tool for Storytellers as well! They're one part of the game where players are directly encouraged to come up with an NPC for you to inject life into the game, and since it's automatically important to them both narratively and mechanically, you can expect a certain amount of investment. That's amazing! I recently did a short Chronicle for just two players, where we played from just before they were taken (allowing some interaction with the Touchstones and other NPCs when they were still &quot;normal&quot;), through the Durance as a prologue (no dice rolls) and then started the &quot;real&quot; game with them just coming back from Arcadia.<br /> <br /> They didn't know what happened to their friends (including Touchstones) in the intervening time, so apart from first trying to find out what year it was, getting shelter, getting clothes to not look like they'd just fallen out of a hedge (let alone -the- Hedge! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ), finding out what was up with those NPCs they had known and their Touchstones was pretty important to them. To further reinforce that, I ruled that their Touchstones counted as &quot;not attached&quot; until they found them again. They quickly found out that their touchstones (which had been with them when they were taken by their Keeper, both PCs had the same one) had been quite affected by their abduction. One of them had been put in a dream coma by the Keeper when she tried to get in her way, the other had become a social recluse due to the fear of fae creatures that apparently could just appear and snatch you, and the two fetches she knew were fake with nobody believing her.<br /> <br /> There was also a third NPC friend (but not touchstone yet, though great candidate for future second touchstone) who had followed the pair into the Hedge to fulfil a promise and became Fae-Touched, but got lost there and had been surviving in the Hedge for what was years (on Ironsides at least).<br /> <br /> So just the Touchstones were already enabling me to give them soooo much material to work with! An oneiromancy dream rescue to undertake, a missing friend in the Hedge, rehabilitating a friend... I then made both of the fetches problematic in completely opposite ways, sprinkled in some other issues with reconnecting with their parents and such, and added an overarching plot...<br /> <br /> There was no chance those two were going to be stuck with nothing to do, their main problem was finding time to do all of it. xD<br /> <br /> Fetches, Touchstones, Pledges, simple things like pre-durance friends and family... all set up interactions with the mortal world, and you don't need merit dots necessarily! No merit dots were spent in the tale above. ^^ Your first Touchstone is free, after all, and you don't really <i>need</i> another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Homebrew</b><br /> - CtL 2E: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1290961-additional-seeming-benefits-for-contracts-2e?p=1454478#post1454478\" target=\"_blank\">Seeming Benefits for every Contract</a>","edited":{"userid":1292,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","user":"Unahim","date":". 12-16-2019, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1292-unahim","name":"Unahim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1292_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1080"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}